        "paragraph_id": "55AA41F4",
        "text": "Turbulence"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 17999,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 511,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 443,
        "paragraph_id": "7FB12346",
        "text": "Wave breaking induced turbulence at the water surface has to be transported towards the bed in order to affect the up-stirring of sediment. Roelvink and Stive (1989) used an exponential decay model with the mixing length proportional to Hrms to estimate the time averaged turbulence energy at the bed from turbulence at the water surface:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 18133,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 515,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 447,
        "paragraph_id": "581C6EE7",
        "text": "where kb is turbulence variance at the bed and k is the time averaged turbulence variance at the water surface."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 18175,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 517,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 449,
        "paragraph_id": "46CB03EE",
        "text": "There are three possibilities for the turbulence variance at the bed (kb) implemented into XBeach:"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
